"""fig3i_bold_r_paired_tests.csv | main Fig. 3 (04_figures/fig.3/fig3_main_A4_v2.py)

Recovered statistical-analysis script | reproducibility package | Fig. 3 track.

WHAT THIS SCRIPT COMPUTES
    This code loads a table of BOLD simulation-model correlation values,
    keeping only subject rows and columns whose names contain the marker
    for simulation conditions, renaming those columns to short model-size
    labels via XLMAP, and coercing the values to numeric. For six
    predefined pairs of model conditions, it computes the per-subject
    difference between the two conditions, then runs a paired t-test and a
    Wilcoxon signed-rank test on the paired values across subjects. One
    row of the output table corresponds to one such comparison pair,
    reporting the pair label, the mean of the per-subject differences, the
    t-test p value, the Wilcoxon p value, and the number of paired
    subjects used in that comparison.

INPUT FILES
    /Users/yunman/Desktop/submission/revision/model_scale_consistent/manuscript_numbers_newflow/3m_model_new_run/baseline同化区域BOLD_r总表.xlsx

